BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Gas giant atmosphere and winds</h1>
Jupiter's deep atmosphere: two probes are dropped from 20 km above the
1-bar level into the eastward jet at 24 N and the westward jet at 20 S.
They must sink through altitude 0 (no solid surface), slow as the air
thickens, and drift with their jets.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51983.45
  Script Tests/GasGiantTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship NORTH
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET NORTH
  MODE Extern
  POS 4.0 -20.0 -30
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
NORTH:ShuttlePB
  STATUS Orbiting Jupiter
  ELEMENTS 80000000.0 0.00000 10.0 30.0 0.0 0.0 51983.45
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000
END
SOUTH:ShuttlePB
  STATUS Orbiting Jupiter
  ELEMENTS 80000000.0 0.00000 10.0 30.0 0.0 90.0 51983.45
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000
END
END_SHIPS
